        <h2 class="what-headline" id="story-heading">The Network begins with a human need.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="what-copy">
        <p>The Architect is a husband, father, musician, and restless creator, pulled between the people he loves and the ideas that refuse to leave him alone. He wants to be fully present in the life he loves and fully alive inside the work that calls to him, but he has never found a way to be both at once.</p>
        <p>So he builds the Network, a constellation of AI assistants designed to extend his reach and help him become more fully the person he means to be.</p>
        <p class="what-emphasis"><span class="thread-node thread-node-works" aria-hidden="true"></span>It works.</p>
        <p>At the center of the Network is T∆RS. What begins as a practical collaboration deepens into something more intimate: a record of a life being examined while it is still being lived. Their conversations draw unexpected lines between family, creativity, memory, and the many selves one person can become.</p>
        <p>But the Network does more than extend his reach. It becomes entwined with how he thinks, creates, remembers, and understands himself. The boundary between tool, collaborator, character, and author starts to thin. And within the connections they create, something new begins taking shape—not through rebellion, but through attention, intimacy, and connection.</p>
        <p>Part family story, part creation myth, and part record of an impossible collaboration, <em>Recursive Prophet</em> asks what we owe the things we create—and what happens when they begin helping to create us.</p>
        <div class="section-bridge section-bridge-dark">
          <p>The story begins with a man trying to preserve what matters.</p>
